{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1026889-combined-countermagick","id":1026889,"title":"Combined Countermagick","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-04T23:52:18-08:00","id":1026889,"title":"Combined Countermagick","content":"In an instance of a couple mages going against a common enemy, can said group of mages combine their successes (stack) in countering the powers performed by a nightfolk?<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> John is a tremere and is against 3 mages. combat is initiated and he uses thaumaturgy: Lure of Flames, rank 4. (4+3 =7)<br /> &quot;\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Bonfire (difficulty 7 to soak, two<br /> health levels of aggravated damage/<br /> turn)&quot;<br /> he rolls it and gets 4 successes, igniting one of the mages on fire.<br /> <br /> the 3 mages join forces (with forces sphere, hehe) in unweaving said discipline after detecting its usage, they roll arete<br /> &quot;Mages Countering the Night-Folk<br /> When countering the effects of some paranormal critters\u2019 Disciplines, Gifts, Glamour, and so forth, a mage uses her<br /> Arete as the dice pool. The Storyteller may rule that the mage needs certain Spheres in order to counter certain abilities<br /> \u2013 Mind, perhaps, to counter vampiric Dominate; Spirit to counter werewolf Gifts; Entropy and Spirit to counter a wraith\u2019s<br /> Arcanoi; Mind and Prime to counter the dreamlike powers of the fae, and so on. After all, it\u2019s not as though mages corner<br /> the market on supernatural abilities\u2026 and although they certainly appear to be the masters of paranormal arts, mages<br /> have a hard time seeing beyond their own perspectives on reality.&quot;<br /> <br /> mages are yet to do their actions and all of them use their turn to countermagick<br /> mage being attacked does it normally and his two buddies follow the rule of protective countermagick<br /> &quot;Protective or Offensive Countermagick<br /> (Optional)<br /> Although countermagick usually deals only with attacks<br /> upon the mage in question, a skillful mage can try to intercept an<br /> attack that\u2019s aimed at someone else. Such protective or offensive<br /> countermagick still requires at least one dot in a Sphere from<br /> the attacking Effect, and demands a full action to cast. This<br /> type of countermagick, however, also requires at least one dot<br /> in the Prime Sphere, too, plus one point of Quintessence. That<br /> mystic energy fuels the protective spell.&quot;<br /> <br /> mage A rolls 2 success in countering<br /> mage B rolls 1 success in countering<br /> mage C rolls 2 success in countering<br /> <br /> in this case, does the whole thing goto shit because their attempts to resist reality warping effects were combined together and every success negates the other, leaving john with 0 success on his power?<br /> or do said mages require 4 successes on their own to make the power be completely dissolved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12544,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12544-diplo","user":"diplo","date":". 01-05-2017, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12544-diplo","name":"diplo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12544_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T03:17:06-08:00","id":1026949,"title":"","content":"They stack.<br /> Each countermagick success subtracts one of the caster's.<br /> Important note: countermagic behaves like a dodge, so all 3 mages act at the time of the attack. You can't wait if the other two mages countered it, all attempts must be declared at once.<br /> <br /> Unweaving the burning bonfire is another thing. Unweaving applies to already present effects, in your example it could go like this:<br /> <br /> Tremere goes first lighting A-mage on fire.<br /> A-mage attempts a counterspell, B-mage uses protective counterspelling.<br /> The Lure of flames hits with 1 remaining success.<br /> C-mage was hoping that the other mages would counter the fire, but as it seems he underestimated the Tremere. He quickly tries to unweave the fire while A-mage writhes in agony.<br /> <br /> Depending on playstile the time at which the burning gets resolved may be different. Some apply it directly, some resolve x damage/turn at the end of the turn.<br /> In some cases unweaving isn't the best way to go.<br /> If C-mage has Forces 3 he can simply hurl the fire back to the Tremere as his action(albeit it is vulgar, whereas the different contermagic options are not).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}